# THE DAEMON PROOFS, restored to buck2 (#82 fallout). These 17 were built and RUN by
# checks.server, which went out with the cmake removal because it was fed by the cmake
# duct-tape package. That silently dropped 17 runtime proofs of the Rust daemon: Mach ports,
# mach_msg, blocking receive, the guest-memory hooks, the generated RPC dispatch, per-guest
# routing, persistent threads and the four daemon capstones. They were never dead code; they
# just had no buck2 target because cargo built them. Same shape as scheduler_demo above.

